ause  that is emerging as lingua franca of  South Asia due to Hindi movies or  television programmes or whatever then  of course there are languages different  languages of the country so in my book I  argue that essentially something  patterned after India especially South  India what we need is a three language  policy at the center you have English  Nepali and one of the regional languages  when you go to now that will will be  going into a federal system so  provincial government where you have  Nepali and one regional language and  many local languages  then you go to the local government unit  where you have Nepali one regional  language and dominant local language of  the region this way we'll be able to  manage linguistic diversity of the  country and this will be I think a  contribution where languages are dying  all over the world  almost they say linguistic genocide so  it will be slightly more expensive but  worth the effort because it will  integrate the country in a commonality  well they still have their distinctive  identity is intact plus it will save  several languages from dying down so  this is one of the proposals that I  make in my new definition of Nepali  ahuna lie or the ways of being Nepalese  Nepal has not been getting the attention  it requires I think mainly because it is  surrounded by two of the largest country  of the world to the east west and south  we have India a billion plus country and  to the north even though it's Tibet  Autonomous Region but essentially  People's Republic of China which is  another billion-plus country when you  are surrounded by billion plus countries  you tend to forget that 27 million  people makes Nepal one of the 50 biggest  countries in the world out of 200 or so  UN member countries so Nepal in itself  is not as small as it appears that is by  size of Rafi or population it's one of  the 50 largest country of the world  second if you were to draw diagonal  lines on a map of Asia you'll find that  Nepal is close to the center so apart  from being a transitional space between  the great Indian civilization and  thiboutot Chinese civilization  and also the East Asian civilization of  Burma Thailand and the West Asian  civilization from which extends from  Persia Arabia through Afghanistan  Kashmir so it's a meeting point of  cultures and civilizations that is its  cultural civilizational significance the  third sociological significance because  it has got so much diversity that it  becomes some kind of a political social  laboratory where you can observe things  from very close and then of course this  political challenge in Nepal multi of  multiple transitions from monarchy to  Republic from Hindu religious state to a  secular state from a plant controlled  economy to open economy  unified unitary society to a plural  society from a unitary system to a  federal system so no matter what kind of  political experiment interests you it is  being tried out in Nepal and it's  lessons will be useful for you know  anywhere in the world  because essentially if you human beings  are political animal they are political  animal anywhere if they are social  animal they are social animal anywhere  and the fifth point which I think should  attract world attention towards Nepal is  the definition of democracy till now has  been very much based upon the print  culture when this Benedict Anderson's  idea about print making nationality is  based then we had radio culture which  kind of improved this democratic  practices we went to television culture  internet culture now you have this  social media which is likely to affect  practice of democracy and that in a new  setting you in a new setting you see  impacts more clearly so this observation  how it works out in Nepal it will have  useful nations a lessons for almost any  country in the world so I think this is  why Nepal should get more attention from  scholars from students for from we were  interested in climate change or  graphically because we have Himalayas  and the plains or social changes  cultural changes political changes it's  a fascinating place it's one of the most  interesting times to be in Nepal
 

